{"labs": [{"stimuli": [{"id": 0, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "_data": []}, {"id": 4, "type": "audio", "title": "", "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe7n1le02ob02re2aud01", "coverimg": "enpe7n1le02ob02re2img01.jpg", "images": [{"id": 0, "image": "enpe7n1le02ob02re2img01.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Jack</span>: Welcome to another episode of <i>Digging into History</i>. Today, our guest is going to talk about software before computers. Thank you for coming, Mrs. Ross. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mrs. Ross</span>: Thanks for inviting me. Well, I want to start by talking about essential characters in the origins of software. Most people know that the first computer was the ENIAC, made in the USA at the end of World War II. However, what people don't know is that the concept of software was already old by then. It started in the 19th century in England. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Jack</span>: But how? The idea of a computer was too crazy at that time, wasn't it? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mrs. Ross</span>: Not really. One important character was Charles Babbage. He was one of the greatest thinkers of the time, and he was a mathematician with many ideas. He was too privileged since he was able to invest a lot of time working with what could be, in theory, the first computer.", "time": "0"}, {"id": 1, "image": "enpe7n1le02ob02re2img02.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Jack</span>: I know that, at that time, the most common devices were mechanical calculators, they were useful for mathematical problems, and I guess they were the closest thing to a computer. <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mrs. Ross</span>: But they weren't! Babbage worked on something called the Difference Engine. This device was too complex for some people, and the idea was to develop a theory of equations. Unfortunately, it was too expensive for Babbage to complete his work, and he had some problems working with his engineer. He also worked on something famously called the Analytical Engine, which included the use of punched cards.", "time": "59000"}, {"id": 2, "image": "enpe7n1le02ob02re2img03.jpg", "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Jack</span>: What can you tell us about the origins of software and hardware? <br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Mrs. Ross</span>: Dear colleagues, it is important to know that those concepts are older than computers and that many people in history have contributed to the technology of our times.", "time": "101000"}]}, "type": "slideshow"}], "template_override": 1, "_data": []}], "id": 0, "type": "scholar", "exercises": [{"id": 0, "type": "WLC", "stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "img_path": "", "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": " I can talk about essential characters in the origins of software.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can mention ideas about devices that preceded the modern computers. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can exchange information about the origins of software and hardware with my colleagues.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "What do you know about the first computers?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "How do you imagine the first software?", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct"}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "Going Back in Time to Analyze Software", "type": "free_type_text_area"}]}, {"id": 1, "type": "STI", "stimuli_ids": [4], "template_override": 1, "questions": [{"id": 0, "responses": [{"selected": 0, "id": 0, "correct": 0,